.Dd November 9, 2026
.Dt INTEL_ERROR_DECODE 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm intel_error_decode
.Nd Decode an Intel GPU dump automatically captured by the kernel at the time of an error
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Ss "SYNOPSIS"
.Bd -literal
     intel_error_decode [FILENAME]
.Ed
.Ss "DESCRIPTION"
.Bd -literal
     intel_error_decode is a tool that decodes the instructions and state of
     the GPU at the time of an error. It requires kernel 2.6.34 or newer, and
     either debugfs mounted on /sys/kernel/debug or /debug containing a
     current i915_error_state or you can pass a file containing a saved error.
.Ed
.Ss "ARGUMENTS"
.Bd -literal
     FILENAME
            Decodes a previously saved error.
.Ed
.Ss "REPORTING BUGS"
.Bd -literal
     Report bugs on fd.o GitLab:
     <https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/drm/igt-gpu-tools/-/issues>
.Ed
